Leave the aliased linear image initial transition to the first upload.

The General layout policy does not suppress Granite's automatic initial
transition. An undefined requested initial layout suppresses it, while
LinearHost still creates the Vulkan image as PREINITIALIZED. The existing
first-upload transition is then the only PREINITIALIZED-to-GENERAL
transition. Applies to PyroWave 502a3b52 with Granite fb178c80.

diff --git a/pyrowave_decoder.cpp b/pyrowave_decoder.cpp
--- a/pyrowave_decoder.cpp
+++ b/pyrowave_decoder.cpp
@@ -983,6 +983,8 @@ void Decoder::Impl::check_linear_texture_support()
 				info.domain = ImageDomain::LinearHost;
 				info.usage = VK_IMAGE_USAGE_SAMPLED_BIT;
 				info.num_memory_aliases = 1;
+				// The first upload performs the sole PREINITIALIZED -> GENERAL transition.
+				info.initial_layout = VK_IMAGE_LAYOUT_UNDEFINED;
 				info.layout = ImageLayout::General;
 				info.memory_aliases = &alias;
 				*req.out_handle = device->create_image(info);
